  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The equivalent Wheatstone's bridge network of the given circuit is shown in figure. Here,\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/HOCSsMPj1T3xXx6quAK4y7HgGUATTni2X4KZj1lKzOU.original.fullsize.png\"/>\nThe points $B$ and $D$ are at the same potential as the bridge is balanced. So, the $3 \\Omega$ resistance in $B D$ arm is ineffective and can be omitted from the circuit.\nHence, equivalent resistance remains same when $3 \\Omega$ resistor is removed.",
    "image": null
  },
